cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Slidescape in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Slidescape: a whole-slide image viewer for digital pathology"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Valkema
    given-names: Pieter
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7189-4441"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LUMCPathAI/slidescape"
url: "https://github.com/LUMCPathAI/slidescape"
abstract: >-
  Slidescape is a fast, self-contained, cross-platform desktop viewer for
  whole-slide images in digital pathology. It natively reads tiled TIFF/BigTIFF,
  Philips iSyntax, 3DHISTECH MRXS and DICOM images (with optional OpenSlide
  support for other vendor formats), creates and edits annotations in
  ASAP-compatible XML and QuPath-compatible GeoJSON formats, and can convert,
  crop and resample slides to pyramidal TIFF from a graphical interface or a
  headless command-line interface.
keywords:
  - digital pathology
  - whole-slide imaging
  - image viewer
  - annotation
  - iSyntax
  - DICOM
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.50"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
